# Streexpoo Margix: Technical Architecture & System Documentation

## 1. Executive Summary & Project Footprint

### Core Purpose
**Streexpoo Margix** is a modern, full-stack e-commerce web application. It acts as a comprehensive storefront and management system, allowing customers to browse fashion products, place orders, and manage their profiles. Simultaneously, it provides administrators with a robust backend panel to manage inventory (products), track and process orders, customize the storefront visually (banners and settings), and view analytics.

### The Tech Stack
*   **Frontend Framework:** Next.js 16 (App Router) combined with React 19.
*   **Styling & UI:** Tailwind CSS v4, utilizing Lucide React for iconography. Data visualization in the admin dashboard is powered by Recharts.
*   **Backend Environment:** Next.js API Routes (Node.js runtime environment), tightly coupling the API layer with the frontend application in a monolithic repository.
*   **Database & ORM:** MongoDB, managed via the Mongoose ODM (v9.6.1). Database schemas are strictly typed using TypeScript interfaces to ensure data integrity.
*   **Authentication:** NextAuth.js (v4) utilizing a JWT-based Credentials Provider and `bcryptjs` for secure password hashing.
*   **Key Utilities:** `nodemailer` for transactional emails (order confirmations, password resets), `uuid` for unique identifiers, and `jspdf` for client-side PDF invoice/report generation.

---

## 2. Architecture & File Directory Mapping

The application follows a **Monolithic Feature-based Architecture** utilizing the Next.js App Router design pattern. This isolates the backend logic, the client-facing storefront, and the protected admin interface within the same repository.

### Core Directory Map
```text
c:\Users\nasif\streexpoo_margix\
├── app/                  # Next.js App Router entry points & page routes
│   ├── admin/            # Protected Admin Dashboard routes (Orders, Products, Settings)
│   ├── api/              # Backend API layer (RESTful endpoints)
│   ├── checkout/         # Customer purchase flow routes
│   ├── profile/          # Customer account management routes
│   ├── pos/              # Point of Sale interface (Admin/Staff)
│   ├── login/, register/ # Authentication pages
│   └── globals.css       # Global stylesheet with Tailwind utilities
├── components/           # Reusable UI components (Headers, Carousels, Forms)
├── context/              # React Context providers (State Management)
├── lib/                  # Core utility functions and configuration
│   ├── auth.ts           # NextAuth configuration and Credentials logic
│   ├── db.ts             # Mongoose MongoDB connection pooling
│   └── email.ts          # Nodemailer SMTP transporter logic
├── models/               # Mongoose Database Schemas (Data Layer)
│   ├── Banner.ts         # Storefront carousel banners
│   ├── Order.ts          # Customer transactions
│   ├── Product.ts        # Inventory models with variant tracking
│   ├── Sale.ts           # Record of completed sales
│   ├── StoreSettings.ts  # Global store configuration singleton
│   └── User.ts           # Authentication and Role-based access control
└── package.json          # Project dependencies and execution scripts
```

**Architectural Separation:**
*   **Business Logic:** Primarily resides in `app/api/` (Controllers) and `lib/` (Services).
*   **Data Models:** Isolated in the `models/` directory using Mongoose Schemas.
*   **UI Presentation:** Segmented between `app/` (Page layouts) and `components/` (Reusable React components).

---

## 3. Comprehensive API Registry & Routing Mechanics

The routing architecture utilizes **Next.js Route Handlers** (`app/api/**/route.ts`). The API is embedded within the full-stack framework, meaning requests are handled seamlessly by the Next.js Node server without requiring a decoupled Express/NestJS backend.

### API Inventory

| HTTP Method | Endpoint | Purpose |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Auth & Users** | | |
| `POST` | `/api/auth/register` | Registers a new user. Payload: `{ name, email, password }`. |
| `POST` | `/api/auth/forgot-password` | Initiates password reset flow via Nodemailer. |
| `POST` | `/api/auth/reset-password` | Resets password using a secure token. |
| `POST` | `/api/auth/change-password` | Updates password for authenticated users. |
| **Products & Inventory** | | |
| `GET` | `/api/products` | Retrieves catalog of products. |
| `POST` | `/api/products` | Admin: Creates a new product. Payload: `IProduct`. |
| `PUT` | `/api/products/[id]` | Admin: Updates an existing product's details. |
| `DELETE` | `/api/products/[id]` | Admin: Deletes a product from the database. |
| **Orders & Transactions** | | |
| `GET` | `/api/orders` | Admin: Retrieves all orders. |
| `POST` | `/api/orders` | Customer: Places a new order. Payload includes customer details and `items`. |
| `GET` | `/api/orders/my-orders` | Customer: Retrieves order history for the logged-in session. |
| `PATCH` | `/api/orders/[id]` | Admin: Updates order status (e.g., PENDING to SHIPPED). |
| `DELETE` | `/api/orders/[id]` | Admin: Cancels or removes an order. |
| **Store Management** | | |
| `GET` | `/api/settings` | Retrieves global store settings (contact info, logo). |
| `PUT` | `/api/settings` | Admin: Updates store settings singleton. |
| `GET` | `/api/banners` | Retrieves active storefront banners. |
| `POST` | `/api/banners` | Admin: Uploads/creates a new promotional banner. |
| `PATCH` | `/api/banners/[id]` | Admin: Updates banner visibility or details. |
| `DELETE` | `/api/banners/[id]` | Admin: Deletes a banner. |
| **Sales & POS** | | |
| `GET` | `/api/sales` | Admin: Retrieves historical sales data. |
| `POST` | `/api/sales` | Admin/POS: Records a direct sale transaction. |
| `POST` | `/api/upload` | Utility: Handles multipart/form-data image uploads. |

